<h3>About Boeing Supplier Portal Authentication</h3>
<p>When you click the submit button, you will be redirected to <b>exostar.com</b> (Boeing's official supplier identity provider) for authentication:</p>
<ol>
<li>Sign in with your Exostar Managed Access Provider (MAP) credentials</li>
<li>Grant the requested permissions</li>
<li>Upload corrective action documentation</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E3F2FD;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why we need your complete manufacturing documentation:</b> ASLAMO Level 1 findings require root cause verification to the process level. Your PFMEA, control plans, and work instructions are reviewed by Boeing's manufacturing engineers to verify that the corrective action address the systemic cause. The parts traceability report is needed to determine whether escapes reached Boeing production lines or airline customers. The offline_access permission maintains your session during the multi-document upload (full quality system documentation packages are typically 100-300MB). This is standard for all AS9100D Level 1 findings.
</p>

<h3>五、Consequences of Non-Compliance</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Supplier probation:</b> No new POs until finding is closed</li>
<li><b>Delisting:</b> Removed from Boeing Approved Supplier List (ASL)</li>
<li><b>Airworthiness concern:</b> Escalated to FAA (possible AD for affected aircraft)</li>
<li><b>Industry blacklist:</b> Shared with Airbus, Lockheed Martin, Northrop Grumman (via IAQG OASIS database)</li>
<li><b>Financial impact:</b> Boeing business valued at ~$18.4M/year</li>
</ul>

